# A two-stage economy: ore feeding bread.
#
# The chain itself is CLI shape, not an intervention -- the recipe graph is
# structure, and there is no intervention that rewrites it. So this file is the
# BEHAVIOUR half of the experiment and must be run with the shape half:
#
#   ./build/atc --scenario scenarios/two_stage.scenario --chain 2 \
#       --burn-in 200 --months 600 --out output/two_stage.csv
#
# Firm entry defaults to 0 so the single-good legacy world's draw sequence is
# untouched by the feature's existence. A multi-good run wants it on: with a
# chain, a good can be short of producers, and without entry nothing ever
# answers that shortage. It is switched on at month 0, before any agent acts.

atc-scenario 1
seed 1

0 set_param firm_entry_prob 0.05
